<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammad ibn Rashid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1897">1897</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammad ibn Rashid was emir of Jabal Shammar in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> from 1869 to 1897 and the greatest ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidi-dynasty">Rashidi dynasty</a>. He exploited the civil war in the second Saudi state to take <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a> in 1887, and his victory at Mulayda in 1891 made him master of central Arabia. His capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hail">Ha'il</a> prospered from the pilgrim and caravan trade.</p></div>
